# Every text file checks out with LF, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# This repository needs this more than most, and for a less obvious reason than
# the usual one. `scripts/init.sh` copies `template/` into a new project
# *verbatim* — it copies bytes, not git objects. So a Windows checkout with
# autocrlf on gives every file under `template/` CRLF in the working tree, and
# the copy carries that CRLF into every project generated from it.
#
# `template/.gitattributes` does not save you: it travels with the generated
# project and fixes the line endings at that project's next commit, not on
# disk when it is created.
#
# CI does not catch it either. The template's own checks run on Linux, where
# the checkout is LF regardless of what a Windows contributor sees.
#
# So pin it here, at the root, where it applies to the working tree itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# No binaries in this repository today. If one arrives, mark it `binary` here
# rather than loosening the rule above for everyone.
